<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LIMBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Limburg is a province in the Netherlands known for its rolling hills and picturesque landscapes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOORBEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Noorbeek is a region known for its coat of arms, which serves as a symbol of its history, culture, and values."&lt;SEP&gt;"Noorbeek is a village within the province of Limburg, Netherlands, known for its historical and cultural significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VALKENBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Valkenburg is a neighboring town to Noorbeek, mentioned in the context of a potential merger."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAYOR VAN DER MEER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mayor van der Meer is the leader of the village of Noorbeek, responsible for proposing a merger with Valkenburg."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOPHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sophia is a skilled herald in Noorbeek, known for interpreting the symbols and motifs of the coat of arms."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH COUNCIL OF NOBILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The High Council of Nobility is the governing body responsible for heraldic matters in the Netherlands."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAT OF ARMS OF NOORBEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The coat of arms of Noorbeek features a lion above a fleur-de-lis, symbolizing courage, strength, purity, and wisdom."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MERGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The merger is a proposal for Noorbeek and Valkenburg to combine their municipalities, promising economic prosperity and shared resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1819&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1819 is the year when the coat of arms of Noorbeek was formally assigned, marking a pivotal moment in the municipality's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLLING HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rolling hills are a geographical feature of Limburg, providing a scenic backdrop for the village of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOWN SQUARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The town square is the central gathering place in Noorbeek where important events and discussions take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The sun is a celestial body that sets behind the rolling hills of Limburg, creating a picturesque scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VILLAGERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The villagers of Noorbeek are the community members who gather in the town square to discuss the merger proposal."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLEUR-DE-LIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The fleur-de-lis is a motif in the coat of arms of Noorbeek, symbolizing purity and wisdom."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lion is a motif in the coat of arms of Noorbeek, symbolizing courage and strength."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVER CHEVRONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Silver chevrons are a motif in the coat of arms of Noorbeek, symbolizing the three rivers that flow through the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLUE BACKGROUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The blue background in the coat of arms of Noorbeek represents the sky or water, symbolizing the region's connection to the natural world."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOLDEN CROWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The golden crown in the coat of arms of Noorbeek signifies the municipality's sovereignty and autonomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROSSED SILVER KEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The crossed silver keys in the coat of arms of Noorbeek represent the keys to the region's prosperity and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRISP AUTUMN MORNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A crisp autumn morning in 1819 is the setting for the formal assignment of the coat of arms of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH COUNCIL OF NOBILITY MEETING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The High Council of Nobility meeting in 1819 is the event where the coat of arms of Noorbeek is formally assigned."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THREE RIVERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The three rivers that flow through Noorbeek are a geographical feature symbolized by the silver chevrons in the coat of arms."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL WORLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The natural world is symbolized by the three rivers in the coat of arms of Noorbeek, representing the region's connection to nature."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The coat of arms is a significant event that marks a new era of identity and unity for the people of Noorbeek, becoming an integral part of the municipality's daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUNICIPALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The municipality refers to the administrative body of Noorbeek, which adopts and uses the coat of arms in various official capacities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OFFICIAL DOCUMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Official documents are items that bear the coat of arms, representing the formal and legal aspects of the municipality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flags are symbols that bear the coat of arms, representing the national and regional pride of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local architecture includes buildings and structures that feature the coat of arms, symbolizing the cultural heritage of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"History is a concept that the coat of arms represents, reminding the community of past events and traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Culture is a concept that the coat of arms represents, embodying the shared customs and practices of the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Values are a concept that the coat of arms represents, reflecting the moral principles and beliefs of the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community refers to the group of people living in Noorbeek who take pride in the coat of arms and its symbolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0421</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;NOORBEEK&quot;" target="&quot;MAYOR VAN DER MEER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mayor van der Meer is the leader of Noorbeek, proposing a merger with Valkenburg."</data>
      <data key="d5">"leadership, proposal"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOORBEEK&quot;" target="&quot;COAT OF ARMS OF NOORBEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coat of arms of Noorbeek is a symbol of the village's identity and heritage, deeply ingrained in its culture and daily life."</data>
      <data key="d5">"identity, heritage"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOORBEEK&quot;" target="&quot;VALKENBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Noorbeek and Valkenburg are neighboring towns considering a merger, highlighting their close relationship and shared history."</data>
      <data key="d5">"neighborhood, cooperation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;NOORBEEK&quot;" target="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coat of arms is a symbol of Noorbeek's identity and unity, marking a new era for the region and serving as a reminder of its history, culture, and values."</data>
      <data key="d5">"symbolism, identity"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MAYOR VAN DER MEER&quot;" target="&quot;MERGER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mayor van der Meer proposes the merger with Valkenburg, a significant event for the village."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proposal, decision-making"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SOPHIA&quot;" target="&quot;COAT OF ARMS OF NOORBEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Sophia interprets the symbols and motifs of the coat of arms, suggesting a deeper meaning to the design."</data>
      <data key="d5">"interpretation, symbolism"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;HIGH COUNCIL OF NOBILITY&quot;" target="&quot;COAT OF ARMS OF NOORBEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The High Council of Nobility assigns the coat of arms of Noorbeek, a significant event in the municipality's history."</data>
      <data key="d5">"assignment, decision-making"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;MUNICIPALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The municipality adopts and uses the coat of arms in various official capacities, making it an integral part of the region's daily life."</data>
      <data key="d5">"adoption, integration"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;OFFICIAL DOCUMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Official documents bear the coat of arms, representing the formal and legal aspects of the municipality."</data>
      <data key="d5">"representation, legality"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;FLAGS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Flags bear the coat of arms, representing the national and regional pride of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d5">"pride, representation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Local architecture features the coat of arms, symbolizing the cultural heritage of Noorbeek."</data>
      <data key="d5">"heritage, symbolism"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coat of arms represents the history of Noorbeek, reminding the community of past events and traditions."</data>
      <data key="d5">"remembrance, heritage"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;CULTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coat of arms embodies the culture of Noorbeek, reflecting the shared customs and practices of the community."</data>
      <data key="d5">"customs, reflection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The coat of arms reflects the values of Noorbeek, embodying the moral principles and beliefs of the community."</data>
      <data key="d5">"principles, belief"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COAT OF ARMS&quot;" target="&quot;COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The community takes pride in the coat of arms and its symbolism, fostering a sense of unity and identity."</data>
      <data key="d5">"pride, unity"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0421</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
